refentry.refsect1:
&reftitle.returnvalues;
Returns a SysvSharedMemory instance on success, &return.falseforfailure;. An E_WARNING is emitted on failure, for example if size is too small to create the segment, if the system cannot allocate it, or if another process created it between the lookup and the creation.
The segment is not removed when the object is destroyed or when the process ends: use shm_remove. If the segment already exists but was not created by this function, its first bytes are overwritten with the header of the extension.

&reftitle.errors;

 Throws a ValueError if
 size is lower than 1.

&reftitle.changelog;





    &Version;
    &Description;





    8.0.0

     A ValueError is now thrown if
     size is lower than 1;
     previously, an E_WARNING was emitted.




    8.0.0

     On success, this function returns an SysvSharedMemory instance now;
     previously, a resource was returned.




    8.0.0

     size is nullable now.
